/\"Products\" links are at lines 21–39. The footer text and the \"Event Log\" link to `/backoffice/events` are at lines 76–80. The home page, catalogue and product page all use this layout.\n- **Test coverage:** no existing test checks the logo, the header links or the footer. All five scenarios are uncovered today, and no existing test contradicts the story.\n- **Test levels:** `logo-leads-home` is the story's main scenario, so it gets a browser test (Playwright). The other four get tests against the running application in `src/test-integration`.\n- **Nothing needs your decision.** The designed and generated context maps agree about `portal`, and no new page or endpoint is needed.\n- **One finding for the documentation stage:** the header and footer belong to `portal` in its glossary but sit in a shared template outside any Java package, so the architecture tests can't see that ownership.\n- **Glossary proposals:** \"Site header\", \"Header navigation\" and \"Site footer\".\n- **Assumption about \"the same header and footer\":** the plan compares only what this story covers. The cart link, the login/register links and the theme switcher belong to other stories.\n\nThe stage allowed me to read only the story and its listed inputs, and I went beyond that twice. I opened part of `tasks/CAT-04/plan.md`, which is output from an earlier run. I didn't use it for any claim; every file and line cited comes from the source. I also read a few production files (the templates, both page controllers and the sample-data loader), because the plan has to cite the file and line where each behaviour lives.","ttft_ms":2278,"type":"result","duration_ms":86091,"uuid":"ac793e6c-7a74-45ad-9195-eee1e259e47b","ttft_stream_ms":1427,"time_to_request_ms":36,"first_content_frame_ms":1427,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
